# Refined Full-Screen Focus Mode

The goal is to make the Focus page truly full-screen by removing all surrounding UI elements (global header, sidebar padding, and internal header) while restoring the centered "card" design for the focus tools.

## Proposed Changes

### Global Layout

#### [MODIFY] [ClientLayout.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/ClientLayout.tsx)

- **Identify Focus page**: Add a check for `pathname === '/focus'`.
- **Remove padding and sidebar**: If on the Focus page, render the `children` without the sidebar and without the default `main` padding/classes that create the "gray borders" effect.

### Focus Page

#### [MODIFY] [page.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/app/focus/page.tsx)

- **Restore the centered card**: Undo the change that made the content fill the whole screen. Return to the centered `glass-card` layout.
- **Remove internal header**: Delete the `<header>` element (lines 788-793) that contains the "FOCUS" title.
- **Full height fix**: Ensure the container takes up `100vh` without any gaps from the parent layout.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
- **Visual Audit**:
    - Verify the gray borders and "FOCUS" header are completely gone.
    - Verify the focus content is centered in a beautiful glass card.
    - Verify the atmospheric background fills the *entire* browser window.
- **Functional Check**:
    - Verify all focus tools (timer, Spotify, tasks) are fully functional.
    - Ensure navigating away from `/focus` restores the normal layout.
